#: ../../contribute/feedback.md:7
msgid "Providing feedback about the ROCm documentation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../contribute/feedback.md:9
msgid ""
"Feedback about the ROCm documentation is welcome. You can provide "
"feedback about the ROCm documentation either through GitHub Discussions "
"or GitHub Issues."
msgstr ""

#: ../../contribute/feedback.md:11
msgid "Participating in discussions through GitHub Discussions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../contribute/feedback.md:13
msgid ""
"You can ask questions, view announcements, suggest new features, and "
"communicate with other members of the community through [GitHub "
"Discussions](https://github.com/ROCm/ROCm/discussions)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../contribute/feedback.md:15
msgid "Submitting issues through GitHub Issues"
msgstr ""

#: ../../contribute/feedback.md:17
msgid ""
"You can submit issues through [GitHub "
"Issues](https://github.com/ROCm/ROCm/issues)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../contribute/feedback.md:19
msgid "When creating a new issue, follow the following guidelines:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../contribute/feedback.md:21
msgid ""
"Always do a search to see if the same issue already exists. If the issue "
"already exists, upvote it, and comment or post to provide any additional "
"details you might have."
msgstr ""

#: ../../contribute/feedback.md:22
msgid ""
"If you find an issue that is similar to your issue, log your issue, then "
"add a comment that includes a link to the similar issue, as well as its "
"issue number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../contribute/feedback.md:23
msgid ""
"Always provide as much information as possible. This helps reduce the "
"time required to reproduce the issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../contribute/feedback.md:25
msgid ""
"After creating your issue, make sure to check it regularly for any "
"requests for additional information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../contribute/feedback.md:27
msgid ""
"For information about contributing content to the ROCm documentation, see"
" [Contributing to the ROCm documentation](./contributing.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../contribute/toolchain.md:7
msgid "ROCm documentation toolchain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../contribute/toolchain.md:9
msgid "The ROCm documentation relies on several open source toolchains and sites."
msgstr ""

#: ../../contribute/toolchain.md:11
msgid "rocm-docs-core"
msgstr ""

#: ../../contribute/toolchain.md:13
msgid ""
"[rocm-docs-core](https://github.com/ROCm/rocm-docs-core) is an AMD-"
"maintained project that applies customizations for the ROCm "
"documentation. This project is the tool most ROCm repositories use as "
"part of their documentation build pipeline. It is available as a [pip "
"package on PyPI](https://pypi.org/project/rocm-docs-core/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../contribute/toolchain.md:16
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"See the user and developer guides for rocm-docs-core at {doc}`rocm-docs-"
"core documentation<rocm-docs-core:index>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../contribute/toolchain.md:19
msgid "Sphinx"
msgstr ""

#: ../../contribute/toolchain.md:21
msgid ""
"[Sphinx](https://www.sphinx-doc.org/en/master/) is a documentation "
"generator originally used for Python. It is now widely used in the open "
"source community."
msgstr ""

#: ../../contribute/toolchain.md:23
msgid "Sphinx External ToC"
msgstr ""

#: ../../contribute/toolchain.md:25
msgid ""
"[Sphinx External ToC](https://sphinx-external-"
"toc.readthedocs.io/en/latest/intro.html) is a Sphinx extension used for "
"ROCm documentation navigation. This tool generates a navigation menu on "
"the left based on a YAML file (`_toc.yml.in`) that contains the table of "
"contents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../contribute/toolchain.md:28
msgid "Sphinx-book-theme"
msgstr ""

#: ../../contribute/toolchain.md:30
msgid ""
"[Sphinx-book-theme](https://sphinx-book-theme.readthedocs.io/en/latest/) "
"is a Sphinx theme that defines the base appearance for ROCm "
"documentation. ROCm documentation applies some customization, such as a "
"custom header and footer, on top of the Sphinx Book Theme."
msgstr ""

#: ../../contribute/toolchain.md:32
msgid "Sphinx Design"
msgstr ""

#: ../../contribute/toolchain.md:34
msgid ""
"[Sphinx design](https://sphinx-"
"design.readthedocs.io/en/latest/index.html) is a Sphinx extension that "
"adds design functionality. ROCm documentation uses Sphinx Design for "
"grids, cards, and synchronized tabs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../contribute/toolchain.md:36
msgid "Doxygen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../contribute/toolchain.md:38
msgid ""
"[Doxygen](https://www.doxygen.nl/) is a documentation generator that "
"extracts information from in-code comments. It is used for API "
"documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../contribute/toolchain.md:40
msgid "Breathe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../contribute/toolchain.md:42
msgid ""
"[Breathe](https://www.breathe-doc.org/) is a Sphinx plugin for "
"integrating Doxygen content."
msgstr ""

#: ../../contribute/toolchain.md:44
msgid "Read the Docs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../contribute/toolchain.md:46
msgid ""
"[Read the Docs](https://docs.readthedocs.io/en/stable/) is the service "
"that builds and hosts the HTML version of the ROCm documentation."
msgstr ""

